---------------------------------------------------------------------------
External dependencies (not included in this repository)

Stickies itself uses only the Python standard library and SQLite. The
optional search by meaning (`stickies setup`, which asks first) downloads
into ~/.cache/stickies:

- from PyPI, into a Python venv, exact versions checked by sha256
  (requirements-search.txt):
    onnxruntime 1.30.0 (MIT)
    numpy 2.5.3 (BSD-3-Clause AND 0BSD AND MIT AND Zlib AND CC0-1.0)
    tokenizers 0.23.2 (Apache-2.0)
    sentencepiece 0.2.2 (Apache-2.0)
  Stickies switches off onnxruntime's built-in telemetry
  (ORT_DISABLE_TELEMETRY=1);
- the default model, intfloat/multilingual-e5-small (MIT), int8 ONNX, from
  huggingface.co, pinned to a commit and checked by size and sha256.
  Selectable instead: sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2 (Apache-2.0),
  sentence-transformers/paraphrase-multilingual-MiniLM-L12-v2 (Apache-2.0),
  BAAI/bge-small-en-v1.5 (MIT).

At run time it calls, when present: omarchy-shell, hyprctl, and Omarchy's
default agent (`claude`; chat only, with the notes you choose to send).
